// expect: 42
// A PARAMETER SPELLED LIKE A TOP-LEVEL FN WITH A DEFAULT CALLS THE WRONG
// THING. `g` is `apply`'s parameter, bound to `inc`, so `g(x)` is 42. The
// program traps with an indirect-call type mismatch (measured 2026-09-25):
// the judgment resolved the parameter, lowering resolved the top-level `g`
// and filled its default. Renaming the top-level fn answers 42.
//
// Retires when lowering reads the resolution the judgment read
// (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn g(a, b = 7) = a + b

fn apply(g, x) = g(x)

fn inc(n) = n + 1

fn main() = apply(inc, 41)
